//! The shared unlinker `0x801AB640` is not duplicated here: it is the OS alarm
//! primitive [`crate::runtime::os::cancel_alarm`], which the JAI timer code
//! calls directly. Keeping one implementation prevents the two ledgers from
//! claiming the same address.
//!
//! The free-list heads/tails live in `.bss` at `0x80378C10`/`0x80378C90`; the
//! parameter block is `0x8037CDA0..0x8037CE17`, and the DSP task descriptor is
//! `0x8037CD00`. See the Wave 4 section near the bottom of the file.
//!
//! ## Wave 7 - JAS note-buffer families and size queries (`0x801A18A0..0x801A8060`)
//!
//! Wave 7 continues below the wave-5 buffer sets with the three remaining JAS
//! note-buffer families and the mode/size plumbing that drives them:
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role | confidence |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | `0x801A18A0` | [`fn_801a18a0`] | write the JAS mode word | high |
//! | `0x801A18B0` | [`fn_801a18b0`] | read the JAS mode word | high |
//! | `0x801A3420` | [`fn_801a3420`] | stop a voice and report success | high |
//! | `0x801A3460` | [`fn_801a3460`] | byte size of the base voice buffer set | high |
//! | `0x801A3690` | [`fn_801a3690`] | fast voice restart (free, then start) | high |
//! | `0x801A3760` | [`fn_801a3760`] | slow voice restart (clear, then configure) | high |
//! | `0x801A44B0` | [`fn_801a44b0`] | byte size of the auxiliary 4-voice set | high |
//! | `0x801A4540` | [`fn_801a4540`] | start the auxiliary 4-voice note path | medium |
//! | `0x801A4700` | [`fn_801a4700`] | auxiliary 4-voice restart | high |
//! | `0x801A47D0` | [`fn_801a47d0`] | auxiliary 4-voice retry | high |
//! | `0x801A4890` | [`fn_801a4890`] | auxiliary 4-voice abort | high |
//! | `0x801A4EB0` | [`fn_801a4eb0`] | allocate the auxiliary 4-voice buffers | high |
//! | `0x801A5030` | [`fn_801a5030`] | clear the auxiliary 4-voice buffers | high |
//! | `0x801A5160` | [`fn_801a5160`] | free the auxiliary 4-voice buffers | high |
//! | `0x801A55C0` | [`fn_801a55c0`] | byte size of the 3-buffer set | high |
//! | `0x801A5A50` | [`fn_801a5a50`] | re-run the 3-buffer configuration | high |
//! | `0x801A6960` | [`fn_801a6960`] | byte size of the 2-buffer set | high |
//! | `0x801A69C0` | [`fn_801a69c0`] | start the 2-buffer voice path | medium |
//! | `0x801A76F0` | [`fn_801a76f0`] | start the 4-voice sequence buffer set | medium |
//! | `0x801A7890` | [`fn_801a7890`] | sequence-buffer restart | high |
//! | `0x801A7960` | [`fn_801a7960`] | sequence-buffer retry | high |
//! | `0x801A7A20` | [`fn_801a7a20`] | sequence-buffer abort | high |
//! | `0x801A7E10` | [`fn_801a7e10`] | allocate the sequence buffers | high |
//! | `0x801A7F60` | [`fn_801a7f60`] | clear the sequence buffers | high |
//! | `0x801A8060` | [`fn_801a8060`] | free the sequence buffers | high |
//!
//! The three families differ only in their buffer layout: the auxiliary set
//! uses 4 voices with 3 taps, 2 history buffers and one extra buffer; the
//! sequence set uses 4 voices with 2 taps and 2 history buffers; the base set
//! uses the 3-buffer layout already translated by wave 5. The
//! `0x802DCD64..0x802DCD70` register-save thunks hide the incoming `r3`, so
//! every Rust signature takes the object pointer explicitly.
//!
//! ## Wave 11 - voice cost, sequence buffers and JAI block pools
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role | confidence |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | `0x801A00C0` | [`fn_801a00c0`] | read one JAS pool head | high |
//! | `0x801A0E50` | [`fn_801a0e50`] | read the SDA cost base | high |
//! | `0x801A0380` | [`fn_801a0380`] | allocate and reclassify a JAS pool object | high |
//! | `0x801A25C0` | [`fn_801a25c0`] | apply one voice parameter block | high |
//! | `0x801A2B10` | [`fn_801a2b10`] | per-frame voice cost pass | medium |
