// Wave 104 - the last 19 untranslated entries of the `0x80190000` bucket
//
// Wave 99 deferred these as too large, export-dropped or GQR-quantised. This
// block re-reads each body and lands everything whose control flow, calls and
// stores are recoverable. The six bodies that wave 99 called `F`/`G` share one
// pattern: the Ghidra export opens with an `unaff_GQR0` / `ldexpf` prologue and
// closes with `psq_l` loads of `f29..f31` that Ghidra itself marks as
// descending from an unreachable block. Those `psq_l` words
// (`0xE3E10048`/`0xE3C10038`/`0xE3A10028`/`0xE38100C8`) are the removed tail,
// not part of the reachable body; the reachable float arithmetic is complete.
// The GQR prologue is therefore not reproduced, and every such body says so.
//
// The block is grouped as:
//
// 1. the cue/envelope and tempo leaves at `0x80195510..0x801974A0`;
// 2. the two player-SE spawn twins at `0x80197F00`/`0x80198C30`;
// 3. the cue-record publish helpers at `0x8019A6D0..0x8019C370`;
// 4. the cue-state transition and position matcher at `0x8019E080`/`0x8019EA20`;
// 5. the level/pan ramp and the boot callback trampoline at
//    `0x8019EDB0`/`0x8019F420`.
