/// Runs the first-stage `OSExec` loader: pick a boot image and read it in.
///
/// The routine allocates the four boot blocks (`0x20`, `0x800`, `0x4A00` and
/// `0xE0` bytes), probes the IOS DVD device, and either takes the already
/// selected image or queues two synchronous reads through `0x801D2130` into
/// `0x20`- and `0x800`-byte buffers. It then walks the two image directories
/// with the `0x14`/`8`-byte stride, publishes the chosen id into
/// `0x80003194`/`0x80003198`, and reads the image header and its `0xD8`-byte
/// records into the `0x4A00` block before the final launch call.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_801ae0e0` at `0x801AE0E0` (1668 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/801ae0e0_FUN_801ae0e0.c`
/// - `// observed:` the five `r13-0x4FD8` waits, the two directory bounds
///   (`puVar2[0]` / `puVar2[2]`) and the `0x398..0x465` report line numbers
///   are literal.
/// - Removed: the `bl 0x802DCD64` (`__savegprlr_23`) prologue and the
///   `bl 0x802DCDB0` (`__restgprlr_23`) epilogue; both only save and restore
///   non-volatile registers.
///
/// # Arguments
/// None; the image id and the read buffer live in the `r13` words and the
/// `0x800031xx` globals.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing. The routine either reaches the launch hand-off or enters the panic
/// path.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Allocates four arena blocks, opens/closes the IOS DVD device, writes
/// `0x80003194`/`0x80003198`, the `0x80003100` parameter block, the two launch
/// words and the `0x8038E5E0` DVD context.
///
/// # Safety
/// Boot-time only: the arena, the IOS device and the DVD queue must all be
/// usable, and the read buffers must be large enough for the counts the image
/// reports.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - every call, guard, wait and store is literal; the IOS service
/// numbers, the `0xD8` record stride and the `0x801D18A0`/`0x801D1630`
/// argument split are `// inferred:` from the call shapes.
