// `0x801A9CE0` was read as a dead non-volatile FPR write in wave 105. The raw
// word is `0xFFA0004C`, which is opcode 63 / XO 38 / BT 29, i.e. `mtfsb1 29`:
// it sets FPSCR bit 29 (`NI`, non-IEEE mode) and has no stack or memory effect.
// The six 8-byte `mtspr` leaves just below it (`0x801A9BC0..0x801A9C10`) are
// landed individually in the wave-109 section that follows.

/// Turns the FPU non-IEEE mode on.
